paragraph:
&lt;p&gt;Please note that when selecting the appropriate codes for cataract surgery, always indicate laterality of the operated eye using HCPCS Level II modifier &quot;LT&quot; or &quot;RT,&quot; as appropriate. &lt;br &sol;&gt;Bilateral procedures should be indicated by the appropriate modifier for bilateral procedures (-50).&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Modifier &amp;ndash;78&lt;&sol;strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Unplanned return to the operating&sol;procedure room by the same physician or other qualified health professional following initial procedure for a related procedure during the postoperative period.&lt;&sol;em&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Modifier &amp;ndash;79&lt;&sol;strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Unrelated procedure or service by the same physician during the postoperative period.&lt;&sol;em&gt; The procedure could be unrelated because it is performed in the other eye. Or it could be a new problem, not related to the initial surgery of the same eye.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p align=&quot;LEFT&quot;&gt;For purposes of applying presumption of coverage, when the evidence available discloses certain physical and&sol;or clinical findings consistent with the diagnosis and indicative of severe peripheral involvement, the following findings are pertinent:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Class A Findings:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nontraumatic amputation of foot or integral skeletal portion thereof.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Class B Findings:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Absent posterior tibial pulse;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced trophic changes as: hair growth (decrease or absence) nail changes (thickening) pigmentary changes (discoloration) skin texture (thin, shiny) skin color (rubor or redness) (three required); and&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Absent dorsalis pedis pulse.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Class C Findings:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Claudication;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Temperature changes (e.g., cold feet);&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Edema;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paresthesias (abnormal spontaneous sensations in the feet); and&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Burning.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p align=&quot;LEFT&quot;&gt;The presumption of coverage may be applied when the physician rendering the routine foot care has identified the following by using the modifiers below:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Class A finding (Q7);&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Two of the Class B findings (Q8); or&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One Class B and two Class C findings (Q9).&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p align=&quot;LEFT&quot;&gt;For purposes of applying presumption of coverage, when the evidence available discloses certain physical and&sol;or clinical findings consistent with the diagnosis and indicative of severe peripheral involvement, the following findings are pertinent:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Class A Findings:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nontraumatic amputation of foot or integral skeletal portion thereof.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Class B Findings:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Absent posterior tibial pulse;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced trophic changes as: hair growth (decrease or absence) nail changes&amp;nbsp; (thickening) pigmentary changes (discoloration) skin texture (thin, shiny) skin color (rubor&amp;nbsp; or redness) (three required); and&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Absent dorsalis pedis pulse.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Class C Findings:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Claudication;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Temperature changes (e.g., cold feet);&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Edema;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paresthesias (abnormal spontaneous sensations in the feet); and&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Burning.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p align=&quot;LEFT&quot;&gt;The presumption of coverage may be applied when the physician rendering the routine foot care has identified the following by using the modifiers below:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Class A finding (Q7);&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Two of the Class B findings (Q8); or&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One Class B and two Class C findings (Q9).&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Modifier - KX must be used as an attestation by the practitioner and&sol;or provider of the service that documentation is on file verifying the patient has sufficiently symptomatic HF and electrocardiographic evidence of dyssynchrony or sufficiently symptomatic HF with an EF &amp;lt; 50% and a need for frequent &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;RV pacing. &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;For medically necessary CRT in conditions not addressed by this article, use modifier - SC.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Modifier &amp;ndash; GA should be used when the provider wants to indicate that he&sol;she anticipates that Medicare will deny a specific service as not reasonable and necessary, an Advanced &lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white; line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Beneficiary Notice (ABN) Form CMS-R-131 has been signed by the beneficiary and is on file. Modifier &amp;ndash; GA may also be used on assigned claims when a patient refuses to sign the ABN and the latter is properly witnessed. For claims submitted to the Part A MAC, occurrence code 32 and the date of the ABN are required.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Modifier &amp;ndash; GZ should be used when the provider wants to indicate that it is expected that Medicare will deny the specific services as not reasonable and necessary and the beneficiary was not asked to sign an ABN.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Claims for pacemaker claims that do not meet the criteria for modifier &amp;ndash; KX or &amp;ndash; SC should have modifier &amp;ndash; GA or &amp;ndash; GZ appended depending on the ABN status and will be denied.&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;span&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
